::Q1::How can an IDE-integrated AI tool assist with refactoring?
{ 
~It guarantees the refactoring preserves every behavior
~It removes the need to understand the code
=It can suggest structural changes such as extracting repeated logic
~It physically rewires the computer
}

::Q2::What should be checked before allowing an AI tool to send code externally? 
{
=The organization's data-handling and confidentiality policies
~Only the keyboard layout
~Only the monitor resolution
~Only the IDE theme
}

::Q3::How can an IDE AI tool help with an error or warning? 
{
~It replaces the compiler
~It automatically changes production code safely
=It can explain the message and suggest a possible fix using surrounding context
~It guarantees the error has only one cause
}

::Q4::Why might a developer adjust how aggressively suggestions appear? 
{
~The setting controls AWS billing
=Different workflows call for different levels of interruption
~The setting encrypts all source code
~The setting changes the model's training data
}

::Q5::What is a sensible adoption practice for AI tooling on an existing team? 
{
~Expose all confidential files by default
~Enable every permission without review
=Configure access and settings to fit the team's workflow and security requirements
~Disable all developer testing
}